{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"GHSA-fc5q-39xc-vjpf","published":"2026-10-19T18:32:12Z","modified":"2026-11-17T16:00:03.999173557Z","aliases":["CVE-2026-112366"],"summary":"picomatch vulnerable to ReDoS through single-branch repeated extglobs","details":"Picomatch through 4.0.7 contains a regular expression denial of service vulnerability that allows attackers to block the event loop by supplying single-branch repeated extglob patterns. Attackers can provide globs like +(*) or +(*a), which analyzeRepeatedExtglob in lib/parse.js skips, causing exponential backtracking against short crafted strings and denying service to Node.js applications.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"picomatch","ecosystem":"npm","purl":"pkg:npm/picomatch"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"last_affected":"4.0.7"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/advisories/github-reviewed/2026/10/GHSA-fc5q-39xc-vjpf/GHSA-fc5q-39xc-vjpf.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-112366"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/micromatch/picomatch/pull/194"},{"type":"PACKAGE","url":"https://github.com/micromatch/picomatch"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/micromatch/picomatch/blob/4.0.7/lib/parse.js#L287-L307"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/picomatch-through-4.0.7-redos-via-single-branch-repeated-extglob-patterns"}],"database_specific":{"cwe_ids":["CWE-1333"],"github_reviewed":true,"github_reviewed_at":"2026-11-17T15:56:42Z","nvd_published_at":"2026-10-19T16:17:07Z","severity":"HIGH"},"severity":[{"type":"CVSS_V3","score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H"},{"type":"CVSS_V4","score":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N"}]}